'''Ange Lackey''' (エンジェ・ルース ''Enje・Rūsu'', '''Ange Ruth''') is an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of [[Tackey]] that appears in [[Zero Legends]]. They were added in [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Ange Lackey
|image = E 735.png
|first appearance = '''ZL''': [[Crunchy Cookie Canyon|Sub-chapter 22 - Crunchy Cookie Canyon]]
|money drop = 900¢ - 3,555¢
}}

==Enemy==
Ange Lackey is different from other [[Tackey]] variants in that their [[Long Distance]] attack has wide inner-range coverage in addition to having a relatively small blind spot of 450. They have the potential to deal significantly higher damage through a 100% chance for an [[Explosion]] at 600 range. This further extends the coverage of their 50% [[Knockback]] ability (325-875 range), which combined with their high health and somewhat fast attack rate can make them a dangerous foe under the right circumstances.

==Strategy==
Ange Lackey has surprisingly high pushing power for a long distance enemy, but isn't particulary complicated to deal with: Ange Lackey is unsurprisingly countered by [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]], and to an extent [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Catcrates]]. [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] with Knockback Resistance can hold his ground against Ange Lackey in most encounters as well. They usually aren't the primary threat of any stage they're in, but always keep them in mind when building lineups.

