==Trivia==
*Ange Lackey's name may be a reference to [[wikipedia:John Lackey|John Lackey]], an American former pro baseball starting pitcher who first played for the [[wikipedia:Los Angeles Angels|Los Angeles Angels]].
*Ange Lackey's Japanese name, Enje Rūsu (エンジェ・ルース), can be taken as "Ange Luth" or "Ange Ruth", referencing American pro baseball player [[wikipedia:Babe Ruth|Babe Ruth]], who excelled at both pitching and batting like Ange Lackey is stated to in [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]]. It may also be a pun on デンジャラス ''denjarasu'' (dangerous).
**Ange Lackey's [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]] trait may allude to how Babe Ruth was a lifelong Catholic who died wearing the [[wikipedia:Miraculous Medal|Miraculous Medal]], ''[[wikipedia:The Babe Ruth Story|The Babe Ruth Story]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s exaggerated portrayal of Ruth as a literal miracle worker, or the Los Angeles Angels and [[wikipedia:Shohei Ohtani|Shohei Ohtani]], who is also esteemed as both a pitcher and hitter and often considered a "modern day Babe Ruth" or better.
*Ange Lackey is good in thrice as many roles as [[Ackey]]. According to their Japanese descriptions, Ackey is a [[wikipedia:Two-way player#Baseball|three-way player]] ([https://jisho.org/word/三刀流 三刀流] ''santōryū'', "three sword style") skilled as a pitcher, hitter and manager, while Ange Lackey became a nine-way player (九刀流 ''kyūtōryū'', "nine sword style"), which is not a real baseball term.
**九刀流 is used in [[wikipedia:ja:ジェントルメン中村|Gentlemen Nakamura]]'s baseball manga [https://dic.pixiv.net/a/球神転生 ''Kyūshin Tensei''] (球神転生, "Ball God Reincarnation"), where it is pronounced ''kuturū'' ([[wikipedia:Cthulhu|Cthulhu]]) rather than ''kyūtōryū'' and the first nine-way player is Shohei Ohtani. The manga's protagonist, Misuta Towashima, is based on [[wikipedia:Shigeo Nagashima|Shigeo Nagashima]], who was considered the "Sun of [[wikipedia:Shōwa era|Showā]]" (昭和の太陽 ''Shōwa no Taiyō''), possibly inspiring Ange Lackey's bright, star-like projectile.
**Ackey's "three sword style" may also reference how his attack hits three times, but Ange Lackey's only hits four times (main attack + three-part [[Explosion]]), not nine.
*Since Ange Lackey's Japanese description states that they died, they may be the deceased younger brother mentioned in [[Tackey]]'s Japanese description.
*Ange Lackey's projectile bears a slight resemblance to a yellow ''[[wikipedia:Konpeitō|konpeitō]]'', which may be why they debut in a [[Patisserie Parklands|confection-themed sub-chapter]].
*Ange Lackey is the only Tackey variant that can hit units within their standing range. Tackey stands at 400 and hits between 600~850 range, [[Hackey]] stands at 800 and hits between 1,200~1,500 range, and [[Ackey]] stands at 450 and hits between 650~900 range, but Ange Lackey has a standing range of 600 and hits between 450~750 range.

